From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: run tests with BUILD_TESTING

Keep examples tied to the upstream Debug-only policy, but let the test suite use
CMake's standard BUILD_TESTING option so distribution release builds can test
the installed implementation.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 74f9515..ca24e8e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -34,8 +34,10 @@ configure_file(${CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME}.pc.in
   lib/pkgconfig/${CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME}.pc @ONLY)
 
+include(CTest)
+if(BUILD_TESTING)
+  add_subdirectory(tests/)
+endif()
 if(CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL "Debug")
-  include(CTest)
-  add_subdirectory(tests/)
   add_subdirectory(examples/)
 endif()
 
-- 
